description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, read the trace-store response that is currently assigned and then ignored.

At the compose trace emission this file assigns the awaited fetch result to a local variable. Nothing in the file ever reads that variable, so the compose now waits on the trace store and gains nothing from waiting. This edit consumes it, logging the execution identifier the trace store returned — the address by which that execution row can later be graded.

Perform exactly one replacement. Find the sole occurrence of:
    }).catch(() => { /* trace-store unreachable — never fail the compose */ });

Replace it with:
    }).catch(() => null);
    if (traceRes && traceRes.ok) {
      const traceBody = (await traceRes.json().catch(() => null)) as { data?: { execution_id?: string } } | null;
      const emittedId = traceBody?.data?.execution_id;
      if (typeof emittedId === "string" && emittedId.length > 0) {
        console.log(`[feature-compose] trace emission persisted execution_id=${emittedId}`);
      }
    }

Existing guarantees are preserved unchanged: the catch now yields null so the block is simply skipped when the trace store is unreachable, the surrounding catch is untouched, and the 5000ms AbortSignal timeout stays as it is. A trace-store problem still cannot fail a compose.

One replacement, one file. Change nothing else.

